        "profile": "band-contract/file-source/1",
        "format": "frontmatter",
        "content": "---\nname: program-counter\ndescription: Test program counter with explicit roles and outcomes.\nengine: 0.2.0-lab.1\nroles: [requester, counter]\n---\n\"\"\"\nYou run a deterministic counter: the requester sends increments, the counter reports totals, and\nthe requester stops it when done. The counter is used to exercise journal and snapshot recovery.\n\"\"\"\ncontract @infinity mentions 1 => expired\n\n\"\"\"\nYou ask the counter to add to its total and stop it when you are done.\n\"\"\"\nrole requester\n\n\"\"\"\nYou keep a running total. Add each increment you receive and report the new total. The same\ninputs must always give the same totals.\n\"\"\"\nrole counter\n\n\"\"\"\nAdd this amount to the running total.\n\"\"\"\ntype increment\n  by: integer(1..100)\n\n\"\"\"\nReport the running total after every increment so far.\n\"\"\"\ntype total\n  value: integer(0..1000000)\n\n\"\"\"\nStop counting. No increments follow this message.\n\"\"\"\ntype stop\n\n\"\"\"\nCounting is open until the requester sends stop.\n\"\"\"\nstate new\n  event requester -> counter: increment()\n  event counter -> requester: total()\n  requester -> counter: stop() => complete\n\n\"\"\"\nThe requester stopped the counter. Send nothing more.\n\"\"\"\nend complete\n\n\"\"\"\nThe session expired before the requester stopped the counter. Send nothing more.\n\"\"\"\nend expired\n",
        "sha256": "182f09ca0c4db6451ff563843147988f6aa61a7405a488013a597f6fa6c08d03"
      }
    },
